<title>DENMARK: Danisco takes over Norwegian package firm.</title>
<headline>Danisco takes over Norwegian package firm.</headline>
<dateline>COPENHAGEN 1996-10-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Danish food and drinks group Danisco A/S said on Wednesday its packaging division's Danisco Flamingo unit was taking over Norwegian packaging firm Monoplast from Norway's Naering Invest for an undisclosed sum.</p>
<p>The acquisition, which is to adopt the name of  Danisco Monoplast, employs 20 staff with an annual turnover of around 25 million Norwegian crowns, Danisco said in a statement.</p>
<p>--Chris Follett, Copenhagen newsroom +45-33969652</p>
